'''Visa requirements for Danish citizens''' are administrative entry restrictions by the authorities of other states placed on citizens of the [[Kingdom of Denmark]] as a sovereign state comprising the three [[The unity of the Realm|constituent countries]]: [[Denmark]], [[Greenland]] and the [[Faroe Islands]].

As a [[member state of the European Union]], Danish citizens enjoy [[Free Movement of Citizens Directive|freedom of movement]] within the [[European Economic Area]] (EEA). The [[Citizens' Rights Directive|Citizens’ Rights Directive]]<ref name="ReferenceB">{{cite web | title=EUR-Lex - 32004L0038R(01) - EN - EUR-Lex | url=https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/EN/TXT/?uri=celex:32004L0038R(01) | access-date=25 November 2017 | website=Eur-lex.europa.eu | date = 29 June 2004}}</ref> defines the right of free movement for citizens of the EEA. Through [[Switzerland–European Union relations|bilateral agreements]] freedom of movement is extended to Switzerland,<ref>{{cite web | last=Migration|first=State Secretariat for | title=Free Movement of Persons Switzerland – EU/EFTA | url=https://www.sem.admin.ch/sem/en/home/themen/fza_schweiz-eu-efta.html | access-date=2020-11-14 | website=www.sem.admin.ch | language=en}}</ref> and all EU and [[European Free Trade Association|EFTA]] nationals are not only visa-exempt but are legally entitled to enter and reside in each other's countries.

In order to travel to another country, a Danish citizen requires a [[passport]], except within the [[Nordic Passport Union]], where no [[travel document]] is formally required. However, an identity document such as a driving licence is useful.

As of 2026, holders of a [[Danish passport]] may travel to 185 countries and territories without a [[travel visa]], or with a [[visa on arrival]]. The Danish passport ranks{{refn|group=Note|name=Ranking| Using [[Ranking#Dense ranking ("1223" ranking)|dense ranking]].}} 4th in terms of travel freedom, according to the [[Henley Passport Index]].<ref>{{cite web | title=Global Ranking - Visa Passport Index | url=https://www.henleyglobal.com/passport-index/ranking | publisher=Henley & Partner s| access-date=September 11, 2025}}</ref> It is also ranked 3rd by the [[The Passport Index|Global Passport Power Rank]].<ref name=":12">{{cite web |title=Global Passport Power Rank |url=https://www.passportindex.org/byRank.php}}</ref>

