* Danish citizens can enter South Korea as a short term visit (e.g., tours, visiting relatives or friends, attending simple meetings) up to 90 days without a visa, though you should remain aware of the quarantine requirements. You must also have an onward or return ticket. It is illegal to work on a tourist visa, whether as a teacher or in any other capacity.<ref name="gov.uk South Korea">{{cite web | title=Entry requirements - South Korea travel advice | url=https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea/entry-requirements | website=GOV.UK | access-date=3 December 2021 | language=en}}  [[File:Open Government Licence logo.svg|30px]] Text was copied from this source, which is available under an [https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/  Open Government Licence v3.0]. © Crown copyright.</ref>
